[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4019"] :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3{x}^{2}+3{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}$  is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{13})}^{3} & =3(2)^{2}+C \\\\ 13 & =12+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309/selection/ec7a2723785556804d91f951aadd4e34ca5e4e7ec54b5dea15233868f26e6ed8" :answer/id #uuid "952d6638-c733-51a4-82c1-b8f542a4dbcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309/selection/94bcd419c780fb0d4ee825e9dc00cd0b50c78a1165d798073c013a5c745a30a5" :answer/id #uuid "e5f769f3-c488-5e60-8b10-e07de00a892f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309/selection/82eae0ca587d8cedf1f240e052cb85835dc8e0beee9cadb7a9e5e6fb3b430b6c" :answer/id #uuid "01cde3e0-f862-5b29-80fd-e43104620586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309/selection/951ff1eb8c4a1248e882b0ebe8aba260abd43e46309369e85ec7e3af484eb548" :answer/id #uuid "7fc5f637-d6a4-59de-b6d2-103abdf33cd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309/selection/7f648b26b0b0acd27263e37990c04a472995eb012d45c5603d0f0b6b44d0cfe6" :answer/id #uuid "00f9f1a5-f46a-52b5-808c-b763c4421c1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddd55144-c2ba-57a4-82ec-bee36392a6bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8309/selection/94bcd419c780fb0d4ee825e9dc00cd0b50c78a1165d798073c013a5c745a30a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-8309/selection/ec7a2723785556804d91f951aadd4e34ca5e4e7ec54b5dea15233868f26e6ed8" "q-8309/selection/94bcd419c780fb0d4ee825e9dc00cd0b50c78a1165d798073c013a5c745a30a5" "q-8309/selection/82eae0ca587d8cedf1f240e052cb85835dc8e0beee9cadb7a9e5e6fb3b430b6c" "q-8309/selection/951ff1eb8c4a1248e882b0ebe8aba260abd43e46309369e85ec7e3af484eb548" "q-8309/selection/7f648b26b0b0acd27263e37990c04a472995eb012d45c5603d0f0b6b44d0cfe6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8309" :question/id #uuid "65fc80a1-7721-5e98-9055-6f369b27046a" :question/math-academy-id "q-8309" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)} \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\ \\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}=2C.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find ${C}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the above equation as\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055/selection/f06eb13c5457ade7fe03103157454c500e55ee5e73120fa7f2a67490b596f913" :answer/id #uuid "1f1214e9-480e-5e00-9d58-fabbe34483df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055/selection/5edb903ad88c218cda0e7c63977c3f15fd326e134b618b13d2343e48e17e4fc9" :answer/id #uuid "c22f6665-5738-56da-b581-b8d90a921abf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055/selection/5ca686aa78688925967399fc0302fbfb1df961cd6f5db0f28c824ee6754ff409" :answer/id #uuid "13cc58bb-55ce-5b90-bc27-e0d82b697e61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055/selection/48da6881d6c68b519f217fa29f1069d93882a7c1748adafe996442cc65aa793c" :answer/id #uuid "4dc3f3e0-ff57-5efd-bd2a-2ae7c331785c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055/selection/dda578c176ee8f8d07c94471270d249414b8c37ad809db10b548958cebe7e341" :answer/id #uuid "4cf097b4-cf1f-5a26-939d-f3154132a89b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb92c282-cf61-5b85-93a2-fb47c1fb258d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104055/selection/5ca686aa78688925967399fc0302fbfb1df961cd6f5db0f28c824ee6754ff409" :answer-field/choices ["q-104055/selection/f06eb13c5457ade7fe03103157454c500e55ee5e73120fa7f2a67490b596f913" "q-104055/selection/5edb903ad88c218cda0e7c63977c3f15fd326e134b618b13d2343e48e17e4fc9" "q-104055/selection/5ca686aa78688925967399fc0302fbfb1df961cd6f5db0f28c824ee6754ff409" "q-104055/selection/48da6881d6c68b519f217fa29f1069d93882a7c1748adafe996442cc65aa793c" "q-104055/selection/dda578c176ee8f8d07c94471270d249414b8c37ad809db10b548958cebe7e341"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104055" :question/id #uuid "a2470563-1a2f-5e0a-b7d9-e6883d815fd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104055" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104055/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104055"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220/selection/7b9e317a00531c8b82176a43ca6e1e5b6705faa291e73c4b3114aa602ce6947c" :answer/id #uuid "d67abf21-4258-5d25-a6bf-4116fb2dc38a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220/selection/98c33c339a393d32721418e9b7774ea266a80b5fd538dba88c3e1cdca686668a" :answer/id #uuid "ebc01640-f9b4-5f31-9081-7b2cadc0f221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220/selection/fa2ddbd06a97ac38cb8865aa17253954a49371560d33ea55bc3a70b98372e988" :answer/id #uuid "5bb4d639-0119-517a-9dff-02201f38f90f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220/selection/a85b30d7426dde07aba4afaac3e474a92838e53be5d87bf5e6c1211af63b6e42" :answer/id #uuid "d3937128-3f8b-53e0-91dc-8c5fd9f9b870" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220/selection/450a000b8b08077f918dfce214c4e6cb56df899cbc12a08a8419102c643d768d" :answer/id #uuid "4641fa43-5ee8-5a98-a998-8306f96eab45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a51a5481-c1f2-538c-bf44-ea05615e2d8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50220/selection/7b9e317a00531c8b82176a43ca6e1e5b6705faa291e73c4b3114aa602ce6947c" :answer-field/choices ["q-50220/selection/7b9e317a00531c8b82176a43ca6e1e5b6705faa291e73c4b3114aa602ce6947c" "q-50220/selection/98c33c339a393d32721418e9b7774ea266a80b5fd538dba88c3e1cdca686668a" "q-50220/selection/fa2ddbd06a97ac38cb8865aa17253954a49371560d33ea55bc3a70b98372e988" "q-50220/selection/a85b30d7426dde07aba4afaac3e474a92838e53be5d87bf5e6c1211af63b6e42" "q-50220/selection/450a000b8b08077f918dfce214c4e6cb56df899cbc12a08a8419102c643d768d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50220" :question/id #uuid "eab8a97a-f952-5f16-9442-1a3ecf58a82a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50220" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{1+C} \\\\ 1+C & =1 \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50220/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355528/field-1/04aa95a7ea6be88ead3a2a4d793e692429167646e7982c49e05a37b25190881b" :answer/id #uuid "16561ff9-49cc-5c8d-9d91-80496b61032b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x^2+2)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355528/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "abcfd3ba-e3c9-5721-a8d2-3b248e6bea2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355528/field-1/04aa95a7ea6be88ead3a2a4d793e692429167646e7982c49e05a37b25190881b" :answer-field/choices ["q-355528/field-1/04aa95a7ea6be88ead3a2a4d793e692429167646e7982c49e05a37b25190881b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355528" :question/id #uuid "e61295b6-6138-5875-8867-aee2da069121" :question/math-academy-id "q-355528" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\sqrt{y}$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=9.$  Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & =2{x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2} \\\\ y & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+C)^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=9$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =((1)^{2}+C)^{2} \\\\ 9 & =(1+C)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =1+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+2)^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-355528/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355547/field-1/8c78dc31586a8eee17bf8f2c69e800ceeadbc234e10a906a671c8b8a0310b754" :answer/id #uuid "048cd733-c2e8-5560-9a90-750596f21cad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x^2+6\\sqrt{x}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355547/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee9a0b78-99ca-5f4b-a1cb-eda7b77e2f30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355547/field-1/8c78dc31586a8eee17bf8f2c69e800ceeadbc234e10a906a671c8b8a0310b754" :answer-field/choices ["q-355547/field-1/8c78dc31586a8eee17bf8f2c69e800ceeadbc234e10a906a671c8b8a0310b754"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355547" :question/id #uuid "ec860881-ff21-5e4e-8a65-6e52d2f89b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-355547" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(1)=11.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+4x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=11$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =11 \\\\ 6(1)^{1/2}+2(1)^{2}+C & =11 \\\\ C+8 & =11 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{x}+2{x}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-355547/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355559/field-1/a4e588486c29ac8b6a946ccb306e8c4ae5eeae1bb683c6637c4b3a1802424381" :answer/id #uuid "2a0b9fd2-1a98-57a7-aaf0-4cd30a179d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2e^{2x^2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355559/field-1/d1be47c1e787246d07be6f56e1ebe1c63bba7219d8416d33023a76d26b7e8dab" :answer/id #uuid "8738d267-dd21-5b3e-990b-73cdd6fd0592" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2e^{2x^2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355559/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "82fc8af0-57e3-5be9-8c92-d5f15f62151b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355559/field-1/a4e588486c29ac8b6a946ccb306e8c4ae5eeae1bb683c6637c4b3a1802424381" :answer-field/choices ["q-355559/field-1/a4e588486c29ac8b6a946ccb306e8c4ae5eeae1bb683c6637c4b3a1802424381" "q-355559/field-1/d1be47c1e787246d07be6f56e1ebe1c63bba7219d8416d33023a76d26b7e8dab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355559" :question/id #uuid "2c2662fd-a3c2-5d7c-b983-4e24453e056f" :question/math-academy-id "q-355559" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$ Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2} & =4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x{y}^{2}+4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x({y}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1) & =2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExponentiating both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)} & ={e}^{2{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ {y}^{2}+1 & =C{e}^{2{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{C{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C{e}^{2(0)^{2}}-1} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C-1} & =1 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\sqrt{2{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-355559/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064/selection/c622ab28f104062c4bf86dbb8aa4a876aee721e56cdb5f5265fd90c24c4efcd6" :answer/id #uuid "98c45658-526f-5c3d-a7a4-904eaec5c7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064/selection/4f966b991a3374182b0a3e26b3918a46a17f4f4f8eeffa8dce6d2884e6f3b8cc" :answer/id #uuid "4bc12d2e-e51b-5a42-96cd-b305f65fb37f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064/selection/d59e3bd2c1167d422bed496710a282e1ab3c5aaa8daf30da10f1251b5752199c" :answer/id #uuid "eb56b96c-6b1e-5509-9c5c-9596df9d1218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064/selection/f6671838d1dc023c4a8f9a3cab3fbb8623185965e0ea25d280bf865c8f85860e" :answer/id #uuid "9123b0fe-37e0-53a2-b9b6-a4027f596f01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064/selection/75291421b2e0d70a537a008b349571f445c281bcb855963d1ce5ecca08b0234c" :answer/id #uuid "db1c7f3a-6ecc-55c5-809a-0863430e9877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "062b6761-8a83-56a7-ab24-c797cc9067ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104064/selection/4f966b991a3374182b0a3e26b3918a46a17f4f4f8eeffa8dce6d2884e6f3b8cc" :answer-field/choices ["q-104064/selection/c622ab28f104062c4bf86dbb8aa4a876aee721e56cdb5f5265fd90c24c4efcd6" "q-104064/selection/4f966b991a3374182b0a3e26b3918a46a17f4f4f8eeffa8dce6d2884e6f3b8cc" "q-104064/selection/d59e3bd2c1167d422bed496710a282e1ab3c5aaa8daf30da10f1251b5752199c" "q-104064/selection/f6671838d1dc023c4a8f9a3cab3fbb8623185965e0ea25d280bf865c8f85860e" "q-104064/selection/75291421b2e0d70a537a008b349571f445c281bcb855963d1ce5ecca08b0234c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104064" :question/id #uuid "76f508a1-f65b-5d1d-8bbf-94be0b492cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-104064" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104064/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267/selection/c960181221795b14ca8f12f4995589f7a3b2d6dd6b0655e8d8228e348c739375" :answer/id #uuid "2c4121d6-bab1-56e1-abd4-3bf6e7a40176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2x-{e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267/selection/e2057dfba16e646c1fccc2fbc71ac24b5435e1d0b0106cddfdd02e5f5c98c695" :answer/id #uuid "8737c814-c6ba-5785-8955-54b94b08fc8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267/selection/e58784f10405fa9a18f2fa34e78a03fc8207e71d28c464b4de05728de30329d7" :answer/id #uuid "b247558b-3f44-596b-8b69-4a7a26fdabe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267/selection/589820737b044a3ce8b4d947bfaeca7e38795de9d22a855e61b73e3e953e9acb" :answer/id #uuid "2e605334-fa8a-5fc8-84ae-745241f7e87b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x+{e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267/selection/37e7a25d321b7befdae25012587fd88190a1483d0acfb4de835ce65927a94012" :answer/id #uuid "c4f4d250-d63c-5e5d-9611-c2c1acc8c318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a2c8b3-5c91-581b-a5a1-77684e23bbb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14267/selection/e2057dfba16e646c1fccc2fbc71ac24b5435e1d0b0106cddfdd02e5f5c98c695" :answer-field/choices ["q-14267/selection/c960181221795b14ca8f12f4995589f7a3b2d6dd6b0655e8d8228e348c739375" "q-14267/selection/e2057dfba16e646c1fccc2fbc71ac24b5435e1d0b0106cddfdd02e5f5c98c695" "q-14267/selection/e58784f10405fa9a18f2fa34e78a03fc8207e71d28c464b4de05728de30329d7" "q-14267/selection/589820737b044a3ce8b4d947bfaeca7e38795de9d22a855e61b73e3e953e9acb" "q-14267/selection/37e7a25d321b7befdae25012587fd88190a1483d0acfb4de835ce65927a94012"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14267" :question/id #uuid "89b29480-9c98-5ccc-8d03-beba2594d431" :question/math-academy-id "q-14267" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x+y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{e}^{y} \\\\ {e}^{-y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{-y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{e}^{-y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{-y} & =-{e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ -y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}) \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{0}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ C-1 & =2 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-14267/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14267"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355577/field-1/eb591616b2fb9e887a317b7f9aeb6c2e0439e4725fccf5669b449d0dac917217" :answer/id #uuid "78623355-e38a-5ca6-82fc-0ede5c4c9a85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355577/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c75e092-6079-5be0-bdeb-81cf428bb1cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355577/field-1/eb591616b2fb9e887a317b7f9aeb6c2e0439e4725fccf5669b449d0dac917217" :answer-field/choices ["q-355577/field-1/eb591616b2fb9e887a317b7f9aeb6c2e0439e4725fccf5669b449d0dac917217"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355577" :question/id #uuid "ed0df24d-07b8-5d65-9f2d-72f21abe2584" :question/math-academy-id "q-355577" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-355577/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-540"] :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-541"] :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
